  "id": "Compound::DB00563 - Disease::DOID:1612",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Methotrexate may be associated with Breast Cancer through multiple indirect pathways. Methotrexate is linked to Retinal Vein Thrombosis, which is caused by Anastrozole or Raloxifene, both of which are used to treat Breast Cancer. This indicates a potential indirect relationship where Methotrexate could contribute to the development of Breast Cancer via the pathways of Anastrozole or Raloxifene. Additionally, Methotrexate is associated with Cranial Nerve Paralysis, which is linked to Paclitaxel, another agent used in the treatment of Breast Cancer. These findings suggest that Methotrexate may influence Breast Cancer progression through different mechanisms, possibly by affecting cellular processes or by interacting with pathways that are involved in tumor development. The evidence is consistent with the hypothesis that Methotrexate could have a role in the etiology of Breast Cancer, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
